Package: wlboard
Version: 0.4.0-1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Aleksander Kutycki <74899889+olekkut@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/olekkut/wlboard
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35)
Recommends: fonts-dejavu-core | fonts-noto-core
Description: Lightweight, customizable native Wayland & X11 virtual keyboard & panel editor
 wlboard is a zero-idle-wakeup on-screen virtual keyboard written in Rust with
 native Wayland floating overlay (zwlr_layer_shell_v1), automatic pure-Rust
 XWayland/X11 non-focus-stealing fallback for Ubuntu GNOME and X11 desktops,
 and smart single-keyboard Wayland input-method mode (zwp_input_method_v1 /
 zwp_input_panel_v1) for KDE Plasma Lockscreen and SDDM login screen. Includes
 a built-in visual Panel Editor (0.5u snap grid), granular Sizes & Fonts
 scaling, clipboard copy/paste and file-manager folder shortcuts, searchable
 28-language catalog, monochrome SVG symbol mode, and JSON User Presets.
